mn118:13.2 starts: such bhikkhus are there in this Sangha of bhikkhus.
mn12:53-55.7 starts: and they eat rice, they eat rice powder
mn135:6.5 starts: abandoning the killing of living beings, one abstains
mn135:7.5 starts: one is given to injuring beings with the hand, with a clod
mn135:8.3 starts: But if instead he comes back to the human state,
mn135:9.6 starts: one is of an angry and irritable character
mn135:9.7 starts: and displays anger, hate, and bitterness.
mn135:10.6 starts: one is not of an angry and irritable character
mn135:10.7 starts: and does not display anger, hate, and bitterness.
mn135:11.4 starts: But if instead he comes back to the human state,
mn135:11.5 starts: This is the way, student, that leads to being uninfluential, namely,
mn135:11.6 starts: one is envious
mn135:11.7 starts: towards the gains, honour, respect, reverence
mn135:12.2 starts: one who does not envy, resent, and begrudge
mn135:12.6 starts: one is not envious
mn135:12.7 starts: towards the gains, honour, respect, reverence
